From: Gianluca Mazza <info@gianlucamazza.it>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a3xx: log GPU state on VBIF halt timeout

Flo's A320 reports a zero VBIF request readback and acknowledgment in
both active-display and blank-display device suspend tests. Log whether
the GPU was initialized and whether its RBBM and VBIF clock registers
were accessible when the timeout occurred. This is diagnostic only.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
@@ -593,5 +593,10 @@ static int a3xx_vbif_halt(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 		DRM_DEV_ERROR(gpu->dev->dev,
-			"VBIF halt timed out: request=%#x ack=%#x mask=%#x\n",
+			"VBIF halt timed out: request=%#x ack=%#x mask=%#lx\n",
 			request, ack, A3XX_VBIF_XIN_HALT_CTRL0_MASK);
+		DRM_DEV_ERROR(gpu->dev->dev,
+			"VBIF diagnostic: needs_hw_init=%d rbbm=%#x vbif_clkon=%#x\n",
+			gpu->needs_hw_init,
+			gpu_read(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_STATUS),
+			gpu_read(gpu, REG_A3XX_VBIF_CLKON));
 		return -EBUSY;
 	}
